  "result": "The concept `drv.motion.turning` passed the gate with **OK** on the second of six allowed runs.\n\n**Body:** the concept holds when the yaw rate's magnitude is strictly greater than `tol`:\n`.cmp (.abs (.measure \"kin_yaw_rate\" [x])) .gt (.param \"tol\")`.\n- The absolute value covers \"to either hand\".\n- The strict `>` matches the parameter's meaning: a yaw rate at or below `tol` counts as none.\n- The body reads no speed or gear, so whether the car moves forwards or backwards makes no difference.\n\nThese all follow from the contract's wording, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses** (`tol` = 1 deg/s, three observations one second apart):\n- **`holds`:** a car rounds a left corner at 5 m/s with a yaw rate of 16 deg/s, its heading turning about 16° each second.\n- **`fails`:** a car drives straight east with a yaw rate of 0.\n- **`blind`:** the same straight drive, with `kin.yaw_rate` declared absent and left unset.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. **WITNESS_FAIL:** in the `holds` scene the car's positions were slightly more than 5 m apart in a straight line, but its recorded path length grew by only 5 m between observations. I moved the positions closer together; the body was unchanged.\n2. **OK.**\n\nThe record needed no repair. The run history and choices are written up in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
